    "description": "A NoSQL database, often interpreted as ``not only SQL`` is a type of database that does not rely on the traditional relational model with tables, fixed schemas, and SQL as the primary query language. Instead, NoSQL databases are designed for scalability, high performance, and handling unstructured or semi\u2011structured data. They typically use flexible data models such as document, key\u2011value, wide\u2011column, or graph.",
